    <div><small>Reached qualified prospects</small><strong id="ed-out-reached">48</strong></div>
    <div class="ed-result-highlight"><small>Potential applications</small><strong id="ed-out-applications">12</strong></div>
    <p>Applications aren't admissions or confirmed enrollments. This model does not estimate acceptance, attendance or revenue.</p>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="ed-section ed-navy ed-principles">
<div class="ed-wrap">
  <div class="ed-heading"><div><p class="ed-eyebrow">05 / EXPERIENCE THAT INFORMS THE APPROACH</p><h2>Program fit comes before lead volume.</h2></div></div>
  <div class="ed-experience">
    <div class="ed-experience-number">09 <small>WEEK FORMAT / PROJECT CONTEXT</small></div>
    <div><h3>Lessons from education campaign work</h3><p>LeadsFlo's founder has worked on Google Ads for Le Wagon Bangalore's nine-week, in-person web development bootcamp. That experience highlighted practical admissions issues: physical attendance requirements, geographic targeting, course affordability and the difference between generating inquiries and reaching suitable applicants.</p><p>That is experience from an India-based program—not a US enrollment result or a claim of verified student admissions. We use those lessons to ask better qualification questions.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="ed-section ed-cream" id="guides">
<div class="ed-wrap">
  <div class="ed-heading"><div><p class="ed-eyebrow">06 / INSIGHTS</p><h2>Practical guides for education growth teams.</h2></div><p>Explore the decisions behind enrollment-focused marketing and follow-up.</p></div>
